  "problem": "What is the remainder of $-6{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+6x+2$ divided by $3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+5x-4?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x+1 \\\\  & 3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+5x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+6x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,-\\,6{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+8x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\,2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+5x-4}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-7x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the quotient is $-2x+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $4{x}^{2}-7x+6.$",
